### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is false. While Dr. Anthony Fauci did co-author (with David M. Morens and Jeffery K. Taubenberger) a 2008 paper titled ["Predominant role of bacterial pneumonia as a cause of death in pandemic influenza"](https://academic.oup.com/jid/article/198/7/962/2192118), published in the *Journal of Infectious Diseases*, which did conclude that most 1918-1919 pandemic deaths resulted from secondary bacterial pneumonia, the paper never mentioned masks as a cause of those deaths. According to [reporting on the study](https://www.cidrap.umn.edu/influenza-vaccines/study-bacterial-pneumonia-was-main-killer-1918-flu-pandemic) and the [paper itself](https://academic.oup.com/jid/article/198/7/962/2192118), the bacterial pneumonia was attributed to viral-bacterial co-pathogenesis—specifically, the influenza virus damaging the bronchial and lung epithelium, breaking down the mucociliary barrier and allowing common upper respiratory bacteria (pneumococci, streptococci, staphylococci) to invade—not to mask-wearing. The claim that the paper linked these deaths to masks is a clear fabrication, as confirmed by [New Scientist's coverage](https://www.newscientist.com/article/dn14458-bacteria-were-the-real-killers-in-1918-flu-pandemic/).